00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:17.330
Can we look at destinations
coming into San Francisco?

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:19.817
RICCARDO MUTI: Oh, so we want
to look at the destination

00:09:19.817 --> 00:09:20.525
is San Francisco.

00:09:20.525 --> 00:09:20.890
MARY PISHNY: Yes.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.307
RICCARDO MUTI: And
so, OK, so what

00:09:22.307 --> 00:09:24.750
are the cities with the
most departures not anywhere

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.550
but to San Francisco
specifically?

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:29.482
So it sounds like we want
to filter to San Francisco.

00:09:29.482 --> 00:09:30.690
And so look how easy that is.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:32.940
I can just go up to
my filter shelf here.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:35.490
I've got a field
called destination.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.360
Destination, city
name, I'll pick that.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:42.170
I can open this up.

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:44.270
And just like that,
I've got a filter.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.375
I can scroll down and
find San Francisco.

00:09:46.375 --> 00:09:48.000
But this is Google,
so let's Google it.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.450
So I'm going to
do San Francisco.

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:51.890
If I can spell San Francisco.

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:52.580
OK.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:54.200
And now I don't need to
uncheck everything else.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:55.992
I can just have this
handy button here that

00:09:55.992 --> 00:09:58.070
says I only want San Francisco.

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:00.620
And just like that-- no
SQL, no where clause.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:04.610
And sub second response, I've
filtered 116 million rows.

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:06.830
The city with the most
departures to San Francisco

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.600
is no longer Chicago.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:09.320
It's LA.

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:13.430
So a lot of people commuting
from LA to San Francisco.

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.965
These charts aren't just charts.

00:10:14.965 --> 00:10:16.340
They're not just
pretty pictures.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:17.840
They are automatically
interactive.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:20.580
And we're making them more and
more interactive every month.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.747
So one of the things that
we're launching just today

00:10:22.747 --> 00:10:25.220
is the ability to quickly
sort any chart that

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:29.930
supports sorting to be able to
sort it right from the chart.

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:32.030
I don't have to go into
the configuration for it.

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:34.580
I could just say, well, if these
are the cities with the most

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.243
